  <releases>
    <release version="0.2.0" date="2026-11-07">
      <description>
        <p>Vumi 0.2 lets you change your playlists and keeps working without the network.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Playlists can be renamed and deleted, and their songs removed with Undo or moved.</li>
          <li>Offline, the library saved on this computer stays at hand, and Vumi connects again by itself.</li>
          <li>Listens recorded while offline are sent once the connection is back.</li>
          <li>The window narrows to 360 px, with large text too.</li>
          <li>A new album page, with the genre and the record label.</li>
          <li>Add to Favorites and Remove from Favorites in every song menu.</li>
          <li>Screen readers announce cards and buttons and follow the player.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.3" date="2026-11-04">
      <description>
        <p>Vumi 0.1.3 starts faster and uses less memory. On a library of 651 albums from a Navidrome server in the local network:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>With a saved login, the library is on screen in 0.22 s instead of 0.45 s.</li>
          <li>While idle, Vumi uses 133 MB of memory instead of 224 MB.</li>
          <li>The start is smoother, and so is the first time Artists opens.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.2" date="2026-11-03">
      <description>
        <p>Vumi 0.1.2 is about speed. On a library of 651 albums from a Navidrome server in the local network:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>While music plays in the background, Vumi uses 0.45 % of one CPU core instead of 6.8 %.</li>
          <li>Search results are on screen in 186 ms instead of 387 ms.</li>
          <li>Album pages open and close more smoothly, and so does a change of year on the Tuner.</li>
          <li>Fixes from a code audit: the screen after a failed login, server errors without a message, the same song twice in a list, album lengths, and Log Out.</li>
          <li>One permission fewer: the media controls' bus name, which Flatpak grants anyway.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.1" date="2026-11-02">
      <description>
        <p>Vumi's media controls (MPRIS) now use its app ID as the player name, and About Vumi links to the new website, vumi.bojanowski.me.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-11-02">
      <description>
        <p>The first release: a fast player for Navidrome and other Subsonic servers, with the library kept on the computer, gapless playback, and similar songs and radio from AudioMuse-AI.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
